01:05:06,684 --> 01:05:22,382
It's not a commentary on the staff at the city hall, but I do not believe that when I look at the statute on school committees, our responsibility does not say a thing about being concerned about the minute municipal financial situation.

547
01:05:23,023 --> 01:05:27,108
Our responsibility is on is the children.

548
01:05:28,554 --> 01:05:30,915
and their education and it begins and ends there.

549
01:05:31,095 --> 01:05:36,116
It doesn't have to do with whether or not the rec department can get more staff or the police department can get more staff.

550
01:05:36,776 --> 01:05:41,378
And I vehemently disagree that we should spend more than a minute thinking about it.

551
01:05:41,938 --> 01:05:46,019
We should figure out what we need for the students and we should ask for it.

552
01:05:46,299 --> 01:05:57,843
And then let the mayor's office deal with whatever communications are required when that office cannot give us the money because of competing priorities, which I think are real.

553
01:05:59,382 --> 01:06:03,484
I don't live in a bubble, I get it, that they're real.

554
01:06:03,624 --> 01:06:10,868
But I just think that we spend too much time talking about and being worried about the municipal government's finances.

555
01:06:11,268 --> 01:06:16,330
We did start earlier with, we have no capacity to raise a nickel.

556
01:06:17,091 --> 01:06:17,891
And you know who does?

557
01:06:18,852 --> 01:06:23,294
The municipal government can raise taxes if they see fit, and they don't.

558
01:06:24,134 --> 01:06:25,955
So as far as I'm concerned,

559
01:06:26,948 --> 01:06:30,089
It's not my concern whether they can afford our budget request.

560
01:06:32,429 --> 01:06:35,830
I I'm just tired of the conversation that I don't mean to.

561
01:06:37,811 --> 01:06:40,131
But you have certainly not trying to bring you Mister Murphy.

562
01:06:40,251 --> 01:06:55,615
But I don't but but Mister so I and Mister if I could just respond very quickly that I think I and I say this as you know as a former school committee chair I I actually don't think we really disagree on that Mister so I think you're correct.

563
01:06:56,145 --> 01:06:59,750
It is your job to zealously advocate for the needs of the school system.

564
01:07:00,251 --> 01:07:03,635
And I mean this sincerely, I appreciate that you do.

565
01:07:04,216 --> 01:07:07,861
And I think I think this committee does its job and I think it does its job well.

566
01:07:08,502 --> 01:07:12,928
But I think what you've heard me say is not that I think the committee should spend its time

567
01:07:13,368 --> 01:07:37,799
balancing the needs of the municipality it's at the school administration has to understand that we do have an a nuanced function not because we want to keep the municipal government happy as much as because we have to operate the district and whatever that appropriation is it is our responsibility to plan for any potential contingency and I think it would be a disservice to the committee and to the community to not be very upfront about that with the community and say.

568
01:07:38,441 --> 01:07:42,304
that we're going to make this work regardless of where it lands.

569
01:07:42,364 --> 01:07:43,524
That's our responsibility.

570
01:07:43,624 --> 01:07:47,147
Now, am I saying we're going to make it work as well as we would?

571
01:07:47,167 --> 01:07:49,748
No, I'm not, because that's not true.

572
01:07:50,069 --> 01:07:52,210
But it is our responsibility to make it work at the end of the day.

573
01:07:52,230 --> 01:07:54,171
And that's just life in the administration.

574
01:07:54,231 --> 01:07:57,734
And I can tell you, when I was in your seat, that wasn't my problem.

575
01:07:57,774 --> 01:08:00,015
And I took very much a very simple stance.

576
01:08:00,736 --> 01:08:04,378
But it is different when the work is what it is.

577
01:08:04,538 --> 01:08:05,559
I will say just one last point.

578
01:08:05,579 --> 01:08:07,100
I promise then this is the last thing I'll say.

579
01:08:08,276 --> 01:08:13,459
The audience that I'm speaking to frankly is not the municipal government.

580
01:08:14,379 --> 01:08:22,303
Every community has members of the community watch the school committee meetings but don't have a direct stake as commonly defined in the school system.

581
01:08:23,244 --> 01:08:35,730
And those members of your community are the ones that have to know that we take our responsibility with respect to fiscal stewardship seriously just like you take your responsibility for advocating zealously on behalf of the kids of Medford seriously.

582
01:08:36,376 --> 01:08:48,941
And I think we have a better chance at engendering the trust and confidence of those community members who don't have that direct stake if they know we're asking only for what we need and for what we know we we can make work.

583
01:08:49,761 --> 01:09:00,565
And at the same time we want to keep them informed about what will eventually need and what how those priorities might develop and that's why we try to be that's the transparency pillar that goes along with the coherence but I know

584
01:09:01,243 --> 01:09:09,169
that there are people in your community that want to know about transparency and there are people in your community that want to know about coherence.

585
01:09:09,669 --> 01:09:18,736
And I think our responsibility is to speak to both so that when the time comes and it will that they're asked to invest more in their schools.

586
01:09:19,296 --> 01:09:22,939
They know that we've done everything we can to spend every nickel they've given us wisely.

587
01:09:23,539 --> 01:09:30,865
And I think that that's sort of my the context in which I you know go over that refrain.

588
01:09:31,408 --> 01:09:33,970
night in, night out of the contingency planning.

589
01:09:34,951 --> 01:09:35,311
Thank you.

